{"id": "EUVD-2026-86968", "enisaUuid": "103938c6-db9e-30a2-a96e-288b6293fbc5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nntfs: treat any nonzero dio zero-range return as an error\n\nntfs_dio_zero_range() returns either 0 or a negative errno from\nblkdev_issue_zeroout(); it never returns a positive value.  The\nzeroing failure check in ntfs_attr_fallocate() therefore never fired,\nso a failed zeroing operation was silently ignored: the loop kept\ngoing, the newly allocated clusters were folded into initialized_size\nand the write could succeed leaving stale on-disk data.\n\nTreat any nonzero return as an error and abort the allocation.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:36:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:14:31", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/56392b0d5290ff2b05fc673bc07803b8ae4cfd1b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/607a9478833db656e7ceac8e9e382fa4acfde545"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pm9x-9ffx-jrqj", "CVE-2026-98137"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.1, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "312c6ba8-c681-39da-955e-982421875d39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "568e3785-5bdd-3dd9-82c6-486a38ef025c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "598a026f-8cc4-3519-ad14-591e4a635086", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "495e90fa334828d4119061e2726af51d0a0fb4ed <56392b0d5290ff2b05fc673bc07803b8ae4cfd1b"}, {"id": "8ad950ee-eef0-34b0-8b76-38255890af50", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "c48915db-801f-3d2a-bc63-56460068d28f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "495e90fa334828d4119061e2726af51d0a0fb4ed <607a9478833db656e7ceac8e9e382fa4acfde545"}, {"id": "ca5ae2ff-7faa-3fd5-99c0-8cdd6cf6c3dc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": 